    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yll4n9k",
      "content": "A Database Management System (DBMS) is software that manages databases — organises, stores, retrieves, and manipulates data. It provides an abstraction layer between data and application programs."
    },
    {
      "id": "y2hd65r",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Concept</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Data</p>",
            "<p>Raw facts without context</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Information</p>",
            "<p>Processed data with context and meaning</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Database</p>",
            "<p>Organised collection of interrelated data</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>DBMS</p>",
            "<p>Software to manage databases (e.g., MySQL, Oracle, PostgreSQL)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Schema</p>",
            "<p>Logical structure/blueprint of database; DDL defines schema</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Instance</p>",
            "<p>Actual data in database at a given moment</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Data Independence</p>",
            "<p>Physical independence: change storage without changing schema; Logical independence: change schema without changing applications</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uxlcjmp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.2 Three-Level ANSI/SPARC Architecture"
    },
    {
      "id": "1ubnz5e",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Level</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Who Uses It</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>External Level (View Level)</p>",
            "<p>Individual user views; each user sees only relevant data; multiple views possible</p>",
            "<p>End users, application programmers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Conceptual Level (Logical Level)</p>",
            "<p>Complete logical structure of entire database; entities, attributes, relationships, constraints</p>",
            "<p>DBA (Database Administrator)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Internal Level (Physical Level)</p>",
            "<p>How data is physically stored; file organisation, indexes, access paths</p>",
            "<p>System designers, storage engineers</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7ed1bqj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.3 Entity-Relationship (ER) Model"
    },
    {
      "id": "zw8hgax",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>ER Component</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Symbol</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Entity</p>",
            "<p>Rectangle</p>",
            "<p>Real-world object (Student, Employee, Product)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Weak Entity</p>",
            "<p>Double Rectangle</p>",
            "<p>Depends on strong entity; no key of its own (Order-Item depends on Order)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Attribute</p>",
            "<p>Ellipse</p>",
            "<p>Property of entity (Name, Age, Salary)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Key Attribute</p>",
            "<p>Underlined Ellipse</p>",
            "<p>Unique identifier for entity (Rollno, EmployeeID)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Multi-valued Attribute</p>",
            "<p>Double Ellipse</p>",
            "<p>Can have multiple values (Phone numbers, Skills)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Composite Attribute</p>",
            "<p>Ellipse with sub-ellipses</p>",
            "<p>Can be divided (Full Name = First + Last)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Derived Attribute</p>",
            "<p>Dashed Ellipse</p>",
            "<p>Computed from another attribute (Age from DOB)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Relationship</p>",
            "<p>Diamond</p>",
            "<p>Association between entities (Enrolls, Works_In)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Identifying Relationship</p>",
            "<p>Double Diamond</p>",
            "<p>Connects weak entity to its owner strong entity</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "iuacbzd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Cardinality of Relationships"
    },
    {
      "id": "3b9smmt",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Cardinality</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>One-to-One (1:1)</p>",
            "<p>One entity in A relates to exactly one in B</p>",
            "<p>Person ↔ Passport; Employee ↔ CompanyCar</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>One-to-Many (1:N)</p>",
            "<p>One entity in A relates to many in B</p>",
            "<p>Customer → Orders; Department → Employees</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Many-to-One (N:1)</p>",
            "<p>Many in A relate to one in B</p>",
            "<p>Students → Department</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Many-to-Many (M:N)</p>",
            "<p>Many in A relate to many in B</p>",
            "<p>Students ↔ Courses; Employees ↔ Projects</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 3: DATABASE MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS (DBMS)",
