    {
      "id": "0cncxa0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Important SQL Clauses and Functions"
    },
    {
      "id": "pvjm3nn",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>SQL Element</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Syntax/Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Notes</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SELECT DISTINCT</p>",
            "<p>Returns unique values only</p>",
            "<p>Eliminates duplicate rows in result</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>WHERE</p>",
            "<p>Filter rows based on condition</p>",
            "<p>Applied before aggregation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>GROUP BY</p>",
            "<p>Group rows sharing a value; used with aggregate functions</p>",
            "<p>Must appear after WHERE, before HAVING</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>HAVING</p>",
            "<p>Filter groups based on aggregate condition</p>",
            "<p>Like WHERE but for groups; after GROUP BY</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>ORDER BY</p>",
            "<p>Sort results ASC (default) or DESC</p>",
            "<p>Applied last; can use column alias</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>JOIN (INNER)</p>",
            "<p>Returns rows with matching values in both tables</p>",
            "<p>Most common join type</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>LEFT OUTER JOIN</p>",
            "<p>All rows from left + matching from right; NULL if no match</p>",
            "<p>Includes unmatched left rows</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>RIGHT OUTER JOIN</p>",
            "<p>All rows from right + matching from left</p>",
            "<p>Includes unmatched right rows</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>FULL OUTER JOIN</p>",
            "<p>All rows from both; NULL where no match</p>",
            "<p>Combines LEFT and RIGHT joins</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>CROSS JOIN</p>",
            "<p>Cartesian product of both tables</p>",
            "<p>n×m rows; no ON condition</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SELF JOIN</p>",
            "<p>Table joined with itself</p>",
            "<p>Hierarchies, org charts, finding pairs</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Subquery</p>",
            "<p>Query within query; correlated vs non-correlated</p>",
            "<p>Can be in SELECT, FROM, WHERE, HAVING</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>EXISTS / NOT EXISTS</p>",
            "<p>Test if subquery returns any rows</p>",
            "<p>Often more efficient than IN for large datasets</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>UNION / UNION ALL</p>",
            "<p>Combine result sets; UNION removes duplicates</p>",
            "<p>UNION ALL is faster; keeps duplicates</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Aggregate Functions</p>",
            "<p>COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX</p>",
            "<p>Operate on sets of rows; ignore NULLs (except COUNT(*))</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Window Functions</p>",
            "<p>ROW_NUMBER(), RANK(), DENSE_RANK(), LEAD(), LAG(), PARTITION BY</p>",
            "<p>Analytics; do not collapse rows like GROUP BY</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0cuh4ey",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.5 Normalisation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ksl1nqy",
      "content": "Normalisation is the process of organising a database to reduce data redundancy and improve data integrity. It involves decomposing tables to satisfy specific normal forms while preserving dependencies."
    },
    {
      "id": "9d2go1m",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Normal Form</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Condition to Satisfy</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>What it Eliminates</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>1NF (First Normal Form)</p>",
            "<p>Every attribute has atomic (indivisible) values; no repeating groups; has primary key</p>",
            "<p>Multi-valued attributes, nested tables</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>2NF (Second Normal Form)</p>",
            "<p>In 1NF + no partial dependency (non-key attribute depends on whole composite PK)</p>",
            "<p>Partial functional dependencies; redundancy due to composite keys</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>3NF (Third Normal Form)</p>",
            "<p>In 2NF + no transitive dependency (non-key attribute depends on another non-key attribute)</p>",
            "<p>Transitive dependencies; update anomalies</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>BCNF (Boyce-Codd NF)</p>",
            "<p>In 3NF + for every functional dependency X→Y, X must be a super key</p>",
            "<p>More stricter than 3NF; handles certain anomalies 3NF misses</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>4NF (Fourth Normal Form)</p>",
            "<p>In BCNF + no multi-valued dependency</p>",
            "<p>Independent multi-valued facts stored separately</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>5NF (Fifth Normal Form)</p>",
            "<p>In 4NF + no join dependency that isn't implied by candidate keys</p>",
            "<p>Redundancy from join dependencies</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1t61tx5",
      "content": "<strong>Note: </strong><em>For exams: Master 1NF through BCNF. The most common exam questions involve identifying and eliminating partial and transitive dependencies.</em>"
    },
    {
      "id": "h67swm0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.6 Transactions and ACID Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Primary Keys cannot accept NULL values, whereas Unique Keys permit a single NULL value.",
        "DDL commands (CREATE, ALTER, DROP, TRUNCATE) are auto-committed, while DML commands (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) require explicit COMMIT or ROLLBACK.",
        "Boyce-Codd Normal Form (BCNF) is a stricter variant of 3NF where every determinant functional dependency must be a Super Key.",
        "Concurrency control techniques like Two-Phase Locking (2PL) prevent conflict anomalies such as Dirty Reads and Lost Updates."
      ],
      "id": "dehcz9u"
    },
    {
      "id": "q0r28ln",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>ACID Property</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Atomicity</p>",
            "<p>Transaction is all-or-nothing; either all operations succeed or none</p>",
            "<p>Bank transfer: debit + credit must both succeed or both rollback</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Consistency</p>",
            "<p>Transaction takes DB from one valid state to another; integrity constraints preserved</p>",
            "<p>Account balance cannot go negative after transfer</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Isolation</p>",
            "<p>Concurrent transactions execute as if serial; intermediate states invisible to others</p>",
            "<p>Two users booking last seat; one must wait or fail</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Durability</p>",
            "<p>Committed transactions persist even after system failure; write-ahead logging (WAL)</p>",
            "<p>After commit, data survives power failure</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "oc59knp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Concurrency Control"
    },
    {
      "id": "z2uyjkr",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Problem</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Solution</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lost Update</p>",
            "<p>Two transactions read same value; both update; one update lost</p>",
            "<p>Locking, timestamp ordering</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dirty Read</p>",
            "<p>Transaction reads uncommitted data written by another</p>",
            "<p>ISOLATION levels; READ COMMITTED</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Non-Repeatable Read</p>",
            "<p>Same query returns different values within same transaction</p>",
            "<p>REPEATABLE READ isolation level</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Phantom Read</p>",
            "<p>New rows appear in repeated query within same transaction</p>",
            "<p>SERIALIZABLE isolation level</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "aodi2r8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.7 Indexing"
    },
    {
      "id": "yyvescu",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Index Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Use Case</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Primary Index</p>",
            "<p>Built on primary key; data file ordered on key</p>",
            "<p>Fast access by primary key; clustered</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Secondary Index</p>",
